The attached image (Figure 5 from npj Vaccines) demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances antigen transport to draining lymph nodes and targets migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs). Panel A shows flow cytometry data indicating the percentage of OVA-positive cells and their phenotypes (e.g., MHCII and CD11c expression) in the draining lymph nodes on day 1 and day 2 after injection with various OVA formulations. Panels B and C quantify these findings, showing that Nano-11 significantly increases the mean fluorescence intensity of OVA within antigen-presenting cells and the percentage of OVA-positive MigDCs, compared to soluble OVA or OVA adsorbed to aluminum hydroxide. This indicates that Nano-11 facilitates greater antigen delivery per cell and more specific targeting to immunopotentiating MigDCs, which are crucial for initiating an adaptive immune response.